[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * There is **no error-return macro** (`RETURN_ERROR`, `goto fail`, …), **no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   error enum**, **no `assert`**, **no `errno` use**, **no `NULL` check**, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   **no `-1` / sentinel return** anywhere in the C source.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `synth_pair` returns `void` — it has **no failure channel at all**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * The only *explicit range checks* and *min/max constants* in the library are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the two clipping branches of the `static` helper `mp3d_scale_pcm`. Those are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the library's entire "rejection" surface: out-of-range samples are not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   reported, they are **saturated**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Everything else that an external caller can get wrong (null pointers,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `nch` values that push `16 * nch` outside the caller's buffer, a `z` buffer
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   shorter than `14 * 64 + 3` floats) is **unchecked undefined behaviour** in C.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Those rows are still tested (out-of-process where the behaviour is a fault)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   so that the Rust translation is UB-for-UB and value-for-value identical.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## The table
