[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Axis 2 — input shapes the code special-cases
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **`z` is strided**: only indices `{0,64,…,896}` (block 1) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `{2,66,…,898}` (block 2) are read. Everything else in the buffer is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   irrelevant — a shape that must be verified, not assumed.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Block 1 reads 15 taps** (`0..=14`), block 2 reads only the **8 even taps**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`0,2,4,6,8,10,12,14`) after `z += 2`; the odd taps are never read in block 2.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Sign pairings differ per term**: block 1 mixes subtraction
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`z[14]-z[0]`, `z[12]-z[2]`, `z[10]-z[4]`, `z[8]-z[6]`) with addition
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`z[1]+z[13]`, `z[3]+z[11]`, `z[5]+z[9]`), and block 2 has two negative
